WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.530
My name is Taiki Kudou.

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.490
In a strange place called 
the Digital World,

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:05.750
I met the Digimon.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.350
I'm gonna become the Digimon King

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.960
and bring peace back to this world!

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:10.920
That's great!

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.190
Things are starting to get interesting!

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.360
And now, my epic adventure with 
the Digimon is about to begin!

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.430
DigiXros!

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.850
<b>Team Bagra</b>

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.850
<b>Enemy?                              The battle begins!                              Enemy</b>

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.850
<b>Team ?                       Team Taiki                    Team Kiriha</b>

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.850
Mysterious
Girl

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.850
<b>Enemy?                                    Enemy?

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.850
Rival

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.850
Protagonist

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.880
My name is Taiki Kudou.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.020
I was suddenly taken to the Digital World,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.220
where I met Shoutmon and 
lots of other Digimon.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.130
And I decided to help them out!

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:03.870
<b>The Rival, Kiriha, Appears!</b>

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:00.290
The Rival, Kiriha, Appears!

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.980
What do you think, Taiki?

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:10.040
Well, I'm not sure... 
What is it, anyway?

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.920
The crest for our flag, of course!

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.070
If we're gonna fight 
in the Digital World,

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:17.220
our team's gotta have a symbol!

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.570
As you can see, it's Brother's face!

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.790
How cool!

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.020
Well? Give me your honest opinion!

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:26.860
I guess it's okay...

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.830
Can't you show more interest?

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.390
This is our symbol!

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.430
Oh, well.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.830
Anyway, this will be our crest!

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.240
This is it.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.750
I want us to hurry up 
and get so strong that

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.060
everyone'll be blown away 
just by seeing this crest!

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.380
Now all we need is a name for our army.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.910
A name... for us?

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:06.160
Thank you for coming, 
my Three Head Officers.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.770
Our emperor, Lord Bagramon.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:12.200
A lovely voice, as always.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.180
The three of you together 
make such a lovely image.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:17.960
You!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.480
Baalmon!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.950
Visitor, this meeting is for leaders only.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.590
You are not permitted to attend.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:34.040
Why don't you just disappear already,

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.370
you filthy Reaper?

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.610
I can see I'm not wanted.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.370
Call me next time you need 
someone bumped off.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.190
Now, regarding the matter of the humans

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.800
who have come to this world.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.570
The blue army again?

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:53.280
Those little pests are 
always getting in our way!

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.090
No, recently another boy has appeared

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.020
with a red Xros Loader.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:03:59.680
What?!

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.280
We cannot have any more humans

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.720
with the ability to DigiXros appearing.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.490
You must get rid of them immediately.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.290
We understand, Emperor.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.820
Measures have already been taken.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.290
I haven't heard of this!

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.290
Are you serious?

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.200
What are these?

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.270
Wristers.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.870
They identify our allies.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.820
They'll be handy when 
we're separated, too!

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:26.610
Hey!

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:29.580
Wh-What are you guys doing?!

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.850
Don't just put that thing on!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.300
You never learn, do you?!

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.870
It's because you messed with 
stuff from another world

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.210
that we got wrapped up 
in this to start with!

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.390
Oh, yeah...

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.630
Sorry. That was my fault.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.200
I apologize.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.260
But that was that, and this is this.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.230
It looks like we'll be 
here for a while anyway,

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.040
so I don't see any harm 
in trying it out once.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.810
Darn it!

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.810
I know you're right, 
but it still makes me mad!

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.350
I've had it!

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:04.250
I can't put up with your 
mindless optimism anymore!

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.960
Wow, talk about strong!

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.600
What's happening?!

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.310
Unbelievable! An enemy?!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.970
No. Look at it.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:29.940
A bamboo shoot!

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:32.420
Are you serious?!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.510
This can't be... No, there's no mistake.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.750
This is the natural disaster spoken 
of in the village folklore.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.550
The Day of Rising Ground!

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:44.460
Day of Rising Ground?!

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:46.960
Let me out!

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.180
Who do you think I am?!

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.760
I control the Green Zone!

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:54.010
Let me out of here!

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:56.840
If you show some remorse, 
I might consider it.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.510
Lord Tactimon!

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:04.350
You know my favorite word, 
don't you, MadLeomon?

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.250
"Perfect."

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.080
Correct.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:14.620
I have already released 
Drimogemon in the village.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.330
This is pretty bad.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:31.200
We should get out of 
this Zone, and quick.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:35.470
Come on, Cutemon. Hang on tight.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:37.340
Hey, where'd you go?

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.250
Oh, great.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.040
Honestly...

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.800
The legends say an active bamboo

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.660
fault line runs under this village.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.170
Once every few decades, the bamboo 
shoots rise from the ground

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:53.490
and engulf everything around the village.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:55.890
That is the Day of Rising Ground.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:59.400
I guess anything's possible 
in another world...

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.630
Still, it's strange...

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:06.160
It's too early to be part 
of the cycle in the legend.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.870
And there are far too many shoots.

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:11.770
Anyway... What was his name, Zenjirou?

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.430
The noisy beanpole.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.650
We've gotta save him!

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:18.840
That's hard!

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.840
It's no good. I can't cut through it.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.320
Stop! Don't shake it!

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.010
Zenjirou!

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.840
That's right, he was 
holding his Wrister, too.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.860
Hey, you okay?

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.230
These things are coming in 
handy already, aren't they?

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.840
Shut up! Don't say that! 
I'm embarrassed enough!

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:36.420
And one more thing...

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.470
What?

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:40.890
I'm scared of heights!

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.450
That's not good...

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:43.510
But we'll save you.

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.140
Just hang in there for now, okay?

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:46.940
How am I supposed to—

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:51.020
Crap! I looked down!

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:53.330
What do we do, Taiki?

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.420
We climb!

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.370
I thought you'd say that!

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.120
I don't think you have time for that.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.710
A-A human?

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:02.790
Who are you?

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:05.160
Kiriha Aonuma.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.570
Reload, MailBirdramon!

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.200
Okay!

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.050
A blue Xros Loader?

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.010
Is that guy the human we heard about?

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:19.810
Hey, Kiriha...

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:22.150
You came from the human 
world, too, right?

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.670
Do you know how to go back?

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.220
Well?

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:30.070
I'll help you with MailBirdramon here.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.120
He totally ignored me...

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:36.730
Hold it. What are you doing?

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.620
I don't need your help.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.230
You don't look like the kind 
of guy who'd help others.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:45.770
Very perceptive. 
I think I'm getting to like you.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.180
I only ask one favor in 
return for helping you.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:50.410
Be my right hand man, Taiki.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.210
What?

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.730
Accept my condition, and you live.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:55.160
Refuse, and you die...

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:59.420
At the hands of the 
approaching Bagra Army.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:01.250
Wh-What did you say?

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.040
A Digimon released underground

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:05.710
by the Bagra Army is emitting energy

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.960
that makes these giant plants 
propagate at an abnormal rate.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.230
The village has already 
ceased to function.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:13.010
There's no escape.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.130
That's...

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.380
It is unusual that I give

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.020
a subordinate who failed 
twice another chance.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.910
Go and redeem yourself.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:27.780
I've been hoping to find 
someone to work for me

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.110
who can also use the power of DigiXros.

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:33.170
If you will be my right hand man,

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:37.060
we will repel the enemy 
and obtain the Code Crown.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.590
Code Crown?

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.840
You really don't know anything?

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.300
All right, I'll tell you.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.830
Hey, just wait a minute!

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.790
I've heard enough of 
your bigshot attitude!

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.330
Taiki is my General!

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.770
He'll never work for you!

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.310
What are you laughing at?!

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:57.580
Don't, Shoutmon!

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.730
Kiriha...

00:09:59.120 --> 00:09:59.640
Yes.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.170
How dare you do that to my Brother?!

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.910
We'll get you!

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:37.270
Oh, don't do that.

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:40.050
If you release Greymon, they'll all die.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:41.400
Don't be silly.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.890
Reload, Golemon!

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:51.360
MailBirdramon!

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.070
Golemon!

00:10:58.440 --> 00:10:59.680
DigiXros!

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.410
Trident Tail!

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:13.760
You've served your purpose. Now get lost.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:19.680
That's terrible...

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:21.860
Stop it!

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.130
This one is promising, Kiriha.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:27.350
His Digimon are no good, though.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:29.700
Wh-What'd you say?!

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:32.370
We have to DigiXros now, too, Taiki!

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.140
That's enough! Stop fighting!

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:36.610
Only one thing matters right now!

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.900
Saving Zenjirou and the villagers!

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.920
We don't have time to mess 
around with a guy like him!

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.930
Can I take that as a rejection, Taiki?

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:47.750
Yes.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.860
I don't want to get close to you.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:53.560
I sense something dark in you.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.390
Very sharp.

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.690
But you'll regret it.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.130
Just scream when you're 
ready to beg for my help.

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:02.290
As loud as you possibly can.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.610
Hey, Taiki Kudou!

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:08.840
Oh, that's right! Zenjirou!

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:11.810
It's the enemy! The Bagra Army is coming!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.790
Soul Crusher!

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.340
Heavy Speaker!

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.460
Rowdy Rocker!

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.350
Please, Taiki!

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.800
We can fight if it's to 
protect the village, right?

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:39.270
Of course!

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.070
Shoutmon!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.110
Ballistamon!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.540
DigiXros!

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:47.710
Shoutmon!

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:50.380
Ballistamon!

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.550
DigiXros!

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.470
Shoutmon X2!

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:07.700
Arm Bunker!

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.090
Meteor Shower!

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.270
Hang in there just a 
little longer, human.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.240
Stay away! You're poking me!

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:23.050
MadLeomon, you...

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.880
Pieces of scum! 
This is our final battle!

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:38.260
Die!

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:45.840
He's stronger than before!

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.880
It's over. Just give up already, Taiki.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:58.210
How filthy.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:02.310
Using the characteristics of the 
land to cut off all retreat.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:03.820
Typical Bagra Army.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.410
You again? What do you want?

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.860
I like watching strong boys.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.030
Well, unfortunately for you, 
he's still weak.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:11.960
He's finished.

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:13.740
I wonder about that.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.780
Akari, help me!

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:17.370
We have to get all the villagers 
together in one place!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.540
I have to go, too?!

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.440
Run! Run!

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:24.480
Cutemon?

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.030
I came to help.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.960
I hate sad things!

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:35.450
Akari!

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:41.620
Wh-Who are you?

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.630
Quit lazing around, you dimwit!

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:45.500
If my Cutemon gets hurt,

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.870
I won't let any of you off the hook!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:49.000
What was that?!

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:49.940
Here he comes.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.270
Drill Buster!

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.010
Drill Blader!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.070
Hey, human girl.

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:01.530
Sorry to keep asking you, 
but take care of him.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.770
You're...

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.200
Dorulumon!

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.190
Dorulumon?

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.750
Don't I... know him?

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:11.320
Taiki Kudou!

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.310
I can't hold out much longer!

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:15.280
Just forget about me!

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.230
What are you saying? Don't give up!

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:18.600
Just get out of here!

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.300
This village is done for!

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:23.570
It's surrounded by bamboo shoots, 
and the ground is glowing!

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:25.690
The ground is glowing? Where?

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:29.010
There's one spot that's glowing white!

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:31.300
<i>A Digimon released underground</i>

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.190
<i>by the Bagra Army is emitting energy...</i>

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:35.110
You did it, Zenjirou!

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:37.220
That's what I call a lucky break!

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:38.580
Starmon!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.550
Pickmons!

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:41.020
DigiXros!

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.680
Let's go, boys! The General calls!

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.560
Yeah! Join us!

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.490
Starmon!

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.830
Pickmons!

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:07.590
Zenjirou! Throw that sword 
at the glowing spot!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.690
What?!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.240
If we defeat the Digimon 
under the ground,

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.120
the bamboo shoots should recede.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:13.750
You take it out!

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:16.090
Don't be ridiculous! That's a monster!

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.350
You're the strongest swordsman 
in Koto, aren't you?

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.480
This is nothing!

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:20.970
Show me how strong you are!

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.310
Your optimism knows no bounds, does it?

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:28.970
Whatever happens, don't blame me!

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:31.800
Koto Slash!

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:36.160
You could have at least put up a fight!

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:39.980
Sorry!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.020
Viva Koto Ward!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.520
What?! It can't be!

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:49.690
Now's our chance!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.360
Buddy Blaster!

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.910
Dorulu Tornado!

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:06.100
If I'm going down, I'm at least 
taking the humans with me!

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:09.160
Behold the last of my power!

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.470
Is he planning to blow himself up?

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.830
Uh oh...

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.250
Taiki, what do we do now?!

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:20.890
It's over! Disappear!

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:24.560
Dorulumon is here.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:25.620
With him...

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:29.260
...we can do that!

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:32.860
Shoutmon!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:33.900
Ballistamon!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:34.830
Dorulumon!

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:39.750
DigiXros!

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:45.980
What? Wh-What did he say?

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.080
Shoutmon!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:53.040
Ballistamon!

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:56.350
Dorulumon!

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.460
DigiXros!

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:33.620
Shoutmon X3!

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:38.260
Wow... This is what we turn into?

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.360
Go!

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:02.870
Victorize Boomerang!

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.540
Did I really just DigiXros?

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.810
Great job, Zenjirou!

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.250
You saved us all!

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.590
Good grief.

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:36.150
Your reckless optimism 
shot right through me.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:39.200
I've lost, Taiki.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:43.590
What's that?

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.770
I never thought Taiki 
would get out of that one.

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:53.870
I must have him.

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:08.800
Darn it! I don't see him anywhere!

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:12.060
If he stayed with us, we could X3 again!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.170
We'll see him again.

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:15.450
I just have a feeling.

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:19.260
But anyway, Shoutmon, 
I've decided on our team name.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:22.160
Really? What is it?

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.400
Xros Heart.

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:25.960
Xros Heart?

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:31.270
I couldn't feel any heart in 
the DigiXros that Kiriha used.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.880
I want us to always have our 
hearts working together.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.650
Not bad. Xros Heart.

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.880
It echoes in my heart!

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.550
But what is this thing?

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:45.320
It's a Code Crown.

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:48.230
Another human?

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:49.730
And not only that...

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:51.430
She's my type.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:52.940
Who are you?

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:54.230
Nene Amano.

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:57.860
Shall I tell you what 
that is, Taiki Kudou?

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.690
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:01.970
<b>Monitamon's Lovely♥ Enemy Search</b>

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:01.970
Searching for enemy data.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:03.500
Dorulumon.

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:06.470
Attacks include Drill Buster, which fires 
the drill on his head at opponents.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:11.720
<b>Drill Buster

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:11.820
<b>[Type]

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:14.640
<b>Beast Type</b>

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.590
It could easily drill holes, too.

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:11.210
Excuse me! Could you fix my door?

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:12.320
Sure!

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:14.650
What is he, a handyman?!

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:17.460
Just when we thought the 
Green Zone was at peace,

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.980
we suddenly end up in a new Zone!

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:22.060
A solitary island rises 
from a mysterious sea.

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:24.710
Oh, no! We're surrounded by 
Neptunemon's Digimon fleet!

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:26.660
We're in trouble right from the get-go!

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:27.900
Digimon Xros Wars!

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.570
You can't turn your back 
on the next one, either!

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:29.570
<b>Upheaval in the Island Zone!</b>
